exercises.solution:
```python
def escape(reals, n):
    p = ()
    for x in reals:
        if all(p[i] == x(i) for i in range(len(p))):
            p = p + (1 - x(len(p)),)
    while len(p) < n:
        p = p + (0,)
    return p
```

Each step extends the current condition into the next dense set, exactly as in the proof of the Rasiowa–Sikorski lemma. Disagreements are never undone, because later steps only *extend* $p$. Over a countable model the same construction runs through all its dense sets.
